  "inspection": [
    "HTTP and native normalizers reject caller-supplied identity and bound request size/depth; authenticated peer identity owns forwarded principals.",
    "The configured authority is explicit and stable. Disconnection or unsupported capability fails closed without page-node fallback.",
    "Current grants are checked at page and authority, queried record scope is checked again, and execute remains creator-only. CSRF and live administrator sessions are checked before effects.",
    "Store durable dispatch acquisition is the only gate into the new door/SOS adapter. Existing operations query without re-enqueue; changed credential/grant/config rejects an unstarted record.",
    "The MQTT target and broker binding are frozen. The active bridge must match; one bounded packet carries the operation and authority IDs. No new replayable dtmf_action event is created.",
    "Dispatcher queued expiry/admission shares a mutex, shutdown cancels queued work and wakes workers, and owned Pending state survives late completion. Node joins its state-loop boundary before destruction; adjacent snapshot callback now checks the existing alive token.",
    "The versioned ABI is additive and owns returned JSON via db_free. Existing shell/rule/legacy one-shot callers are explicitly left weaker in the caller inventory."
